<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were largely unchanged on Friday, with only the two-month and one-year rates registering dips, traders said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR continued to reflect the softness at the overnight money market as banks continue to be awash with liquidity, traders said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR quotes represent the rates at which banks are willing to swap pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  FEB 28		 FEB 27</p>
<p>    1 W		9 13/16		 9 13/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9 13/16		 9 13/16</p>
<p>    1 M		10			10</p>
<p>    2 M		10  1/16		10  1/8</p>
<p>    3 M		10  1/8		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    6 M		10  1/4		 10  1/4</p>
<p>    12M		10  3/8		 10  7/16</p>
<p>    VAL		3-Mar		   28-Feb</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
